1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,271
Fourteen ships entered the

2
00:00:01,291 --> 00:00:03,439
Suez Canal for a one-day trip.

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:05,420
They got out eight years later.

4
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,420
Halfway through, war broke out.

5
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,269
Egypt sank ships to block the canal.

6
00:00:09,289 --> 00:00:11,850
And the canal became the front line.

7
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,940
Trapped in a lake, nowhere to go.

8
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:15,886
Sandstorms dusted them yellow.

9
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:16,993
The Yellow Fleet.

10
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:18,535
Their countries were rivals.

11
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,230
The sailors became friends.

12
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,325
Football on deck.

13
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,392
Their own stamps.

14
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,810
Their own Olympics.

15
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,639
Poland won.

16
00:00:24,678 --> 00:00:27,030
In the end, just two could still sail.

17
00:00:27,050 --> 00:00:28,260
Home to Hamburg.

18
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,082
Tens of thousands cheered.

19
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,190
Part of the cargo?

20
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:32,100
Kitchen clocks.

21
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:34,080
Delivered only eight years late.

22
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:36,090
How many stars for this delivery?
